  "manualAssistanceBody": "Tap Circle on your side of the board, or Hint on Play, for a suggested move. Litch prepares a Hint as your turn begins and can refine it while you wait. While you hold the suggested piece, its Hint destination stays stable; lifting another piece shows that piece’s normal legal moves.\n\nOn Play, use Coaching’s P1 or P2 control to turn help on or off for that player, or hold their Circle button for about one second. Coaching shows help automatically on their human turns.",
  "@manualAssistanceBody": {
    "description": "Turn-start Hint can refine while waiting. Only the suggested held piece keeps its Hint target; another pickup shows normal legal moves. Circle tap requests Hint; Circle hold or Play P1/P2 controls toggle that player’s Coaching."
  },
  "manualAssistanceTitle": "Hints and Coaching",
  "@manualAssistanceTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic: requested Hint and automatic Coaching using their current localized product labels."
  },
  "manualComputerBody": "In Setup, choose the computer as your opponent, set its level, and choose which player it controls. The board chooses its moves; you move its pieces.\n\nWait for its source and destination lights, move the indicated chess piece, and remove any captured piece when prompted. Finish every lit step. In Duck, move the Duck to the computer’s indicated destination too.",
  "@manualComputerBody": {
    "description": "The computer chooses moves and the human physically executes them, including the fixed Duck destination."
  },
  "manualComputerTitle": "Play the computer",
  "@manualComputerTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic: playing against the board computer."
  },
  "manualControlsBody": "Each end has a four-direction D-pad, X, and Circle. In ordinary play, tap Circle for a Hint or X for Undo. Hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup. Left/Right chooses a setting, Up/Down changes it, and X closes the menu. On Bluetooth, move to another item before pressing X to close. Follow the lit controls when the board asks for a choice.\n\nIf the app says “Litch already has three paired Bluetooth devices”, clear its saved Bluetooth connections on the board. In Play, hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup. Use Left/Right to select Bluetooth. At that same end, hold X and Circle together for 2 seconds until the blue-and-orange perimeter animation starts. Release both buttons and wait for 3 success flashes, then reconnect in the app. Your game and other settings stay intact.\n\nIn Litchcraft, Left/Right opens the quick palette and Up/Down fine-adjusts the active color. Tap X for Undo or Circle for Redo. Hold Circle for about one second to switch between Paint and Erase. Use the app to select, add, and play frames.\n\nHold X and Circle together at the same end for about 1.5 seconds, then release to exit Litchcraft. Both individual actions are consumed. Lift the brush and close the palette, then shake the board for about one second to clear the frame. Painting, reconnect, and exit must be finished first. Only the selected frame clears; Undo restores it. You can also shake your device with Litchcraft open to clear the selected frame.",
  "@manualControlsBody": {
    "description": "Overview of the physical controls and a pointer to mode-specific controls in their owning manual topics."
  },
  "manualQuickSetupHeading": "Quick Setup on the board",
  "manualQuickCpuLevel": "Computer level",
  "manualQuickCpuPlayer": "Computer player",
  "manualQuickPlayerEnd": "Player 1 end",
  "manualQuickLightPreview": "The board previews the light squares directly.",
  "manualControlsTitle": "Board controls",
  "@manualControlsTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic for the physical four-direction D-pad, X, and Circle controls."
  },
  "manualControlsRecovery": "Busy? Lift the brush or end the app stroke, then retry. Lifting alone never replays it.",
  "@manualControlsRecovery": {
    "description": "Final Litchcraft physical-control recovery paragraph. Busy commands are rejected, never queued."
  },
  "manualConnectionBody": "Keep the powered board nearby, enable Bluetooth on your device, and select your board in the app. Allow the requested permissions and follow the connection prompts.\n\nLitch connects to one device at a time. If another device is connected, open Litch on that device and tap Disconnect, then try again.\n\nIf the app says “Litch already has three paired Bluetooth devices”, clear its saved Bluetooth connections on the board. In Play, hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup. Use Left/Right to select Bluetooth. At that same end, hold X and Circle together for 2 seconds until the blue-and-orange perimeter animation starts. Release both buttons and wait for 3 success flashes, then reconnect in the app. Your game and other settings stay intact.\n\nFollow any connection recovery shown in the app. For a power or sensor problem, follow the Board health instructions. Use Contact Support in Setup, or the discovery screen’s help option if your board cannot connect. You can review and edit a report before opening an email draft.\n\nIf your board runs custom firmware, it must support the Litch connection protocol to work with the app. Use USB to restore the official firmware, or open Contact Support for help.",
  "@manualConnectionBody": {
    "description": "Use existing discovery, Identify, Board health and Contact Support routes. A report is editable before email handoff; do not imply automatic sending."
  },
  "manualConnectionTitle": "Connect and get help",
  "@manualConnectionTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic: connecting a board and finding the existing support flow."
  },
  "manualDescription": "Setup, play, and help. Available offline.",
  "@manualDescription": {
    "description": "Short subtitle for the local manual entry. Opening it does not need internet or a board connection."
  },
  "manualDuckBody": "Before the first move, complete the normal 32-piece setup and add one extra piece on any of the four empty rows between the players’ pawns. Litch recognizes that piece as the Duck and marks it in yellow.\n\nEach turn has a chess move followed by moving the Duck to a different empty square. Finish both steps before the other player starts. The Duck blocks squares and cannot be captured.\n\nThere is no check or checkmate. Capturing the opposing king wins immediately, without another Duck move. A player with no available chess move also wins.",
  "@manualDuckBody": {
    "description": "Litch Duck rules: initial extra piece on any empty rank 3 through 6; chess plus Duck is one turn; king capture or no available chess move wins. Duck remains recognizable in the topic title."
  },
  "manualDuckTitle": "Duck chess",
  "@manualDuckTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic using the established localized Duck variant name."
  },
  "manualIntroduction": "A practical guide to getting started and finding your next step on the board. No internet or board connection is needed to read it.",
  "@manualIntroduction": {
    "description": "Introduction to the concise offline operating guide, not a claim of a complete chess-rules reference."
  },
  "manualSearchLabel": "Search the manual",
  "@manualSearchLabel": {
    "description": "Label for the offline manual topic and body search field."
  },
  "manualSearchNoResults": "No matching manual topics.",
  "@manualSearchNoResults": {
    "description": "Empty result shown after an offline manual search."
  },
  "manualMovesBody": "Lift a piece to see its legal destinations, then place it on a legal square. If Confirm moves is set to Confirm with Circle button, press Circle after placement. The move is accepted one second later. Timed confirmation happens automatically.\n\nRead a square by its file (a–h) and rank (1–8). Play and Game Review show these labels on all four edges. With White nearest you, a1 is at the lower left. When you swap player ends in Play or rotate the view in Game Review, h8 moves to the lower left. A move such as e2 to e4 still uses the same square names.\n\nFor a capture, remove the captured piece and place your piece on its destination. Castling also needs the rook move. Follow every lit step before the next turn. Promotion defaults to Queen, which is applied automatically after normal move confirmation. If Promotion is set to Choose, use Left/Right to choose a piece, then press Circle to confirm. If the board asks for correction, return the pieces to the indicated squares.",
  "@manualMovesBody": {
    "description": "Legal destinations, timed or Circle confirmation, capture, castling, automatic Queen promotion or explicit Choose with Left/Right and Circle, and correction."
  },
  "manualMovesTitle": "Move the pieces",
  "@manualMovesTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic: physical chess moves and required follow-up steps."
  },
  "manualLitchcraftBody": "Remove every piece from the board, then open Litchcraft beside Play—or hold X and Circle together for about 1.5 seconds at one end of an empty Setup board, then release. Litchcraft never interrupts a game in progress. You can create and save artwork in the app while the board is unavailable.\n\nChoose a color and paint in the app, or touch empty board squares with a magnetic chess piece. Effects applies an effect to individual squares. The active tool tells you what the next square tap will do, even when another panel is open.\n\nOn a tablet in portrait, the tools sit below the canvas. A wide tray shows Color and brushes together, LEDs and Effects in the middle, and Frames alongside them. In a narrower tray, select the section you want to use. In landscape, the tools sit beside the canvas. The arrow beside Rotate moves the tools and navigation to the other side. In a narrow landscape window, tap Show tools or Hide tools to open or close the panel.\n\nAnimation holds up to 256 frames. Tap a thumbnail to select it and pause playback. Add copies the selected frame. Hold a frame thumbnail, then confirm Delete, to remove it; at least one frame stays. Use Play/Pause for playback and the timing value for an exact duration.\n\nTap Fill to fill the selected frame with the active color. Hold that same action for about half a second to clear the frame instead. Hold a color swatch for half a second to fill the frame with that color. Undo restores the edit.\n\nUse Artwork to save, import, or share. An editable artwork file keeps colors, effects, frames, and timing; an image is rendered artwork. Import previews conversion before you replace the current artwork. To leave the live board session, return to Play or use the board’s X-and-Circle chord.\n\nOn the board, tap X for Undo and Circle for Redo. Hold X for one second to erase the current frame; Undo restores it. Hold Circle for one second to switch Paint/Erase. The X+Circle exit gesture takes priority.",
  "@manualLitchcraftBody": {
    "description": "Litchcraft admission, Effects and Animation, 256-frame limit, confirmed thumbnail deletion, tap-to-fill and fixed hold-to-clear, editable files, exit and active-game safety."
  },
  "manualLitchcraftTitle": "Paint with Litchcraft",
  "@manualLitchcraftTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic title for the Litchcraft light-painting feature."
  },
  "manualStartBody": "Keep the powered board nearby, enable Bluetooth on your device, and select your board in the app. Allow the requested permissions and follow the connection prompts.\n\nTap New game on Play, or hold X and Circle together at one end of the board for about two seconds.\n\nChoose Time limit on Play before starting. Use Setup to choose the first-player end, board rotation, and opponent. On the board, hold X for about one second to open Quick Setup.\n\nArrange the normal chess starting position and follow any placement lights. Arranging the pieces does not use clock time. The clock starts when you lift the first legal piece after the board is ready.",
  "@manualStartBody": {
    "description": "Offline instructions for New game, first-player end, rotation, clock choice on Play, and X-hold Quick Setup. Call the round button Circle, not the letter O; retain X."
  },
  "manualStartTitle": "Start a game",
  "@manualStartTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic: starting and arranging a new game."
  },
  "manualFactoryResetBody": "Factory reset permanently deletes board settings and saved-game data. Try the recovery and Contact Support guidance first if you want to keep them.\n\nUnplug the board. Hold only Down at one end while reconnecting power. When the X and Circle lights blink amber, release Down and any other held controls. At the same end, hold X and Circle together for at least two seconds. Releasing either early cancels. If the hold is not completed within ten seconds of the amber prompt, the board boots normally.\n\nAfter a successful reset, the X and Circle lights blink green and the board restarts. Waking from sleep or restarting the board cannot start this reset. If reset fails, keep the board powered and use Contact Support.",
  "@manualFactoryResetBody": {
    "description": "Cold-power reset with fresh same-end X and Circle consent, cancellation, completion and support recovery."
  },
  "manualFactoryResetTitle": "Factory reset the board",
  "@manualFactoryResetTitle": {
    "description": "Manual topic for the destructive cold-boot board reset."
  },
  "manualTitle": "Litch Manual",
  "@manualTitle": {
    "description": "Title and About > Discover entry for the bundled Litch operating manual. Keep Litch as the product name."
  },
  "manualUndoBody": "Tap X, or Undo on Play, then follow the return-square lights. Restore any captured piece when prompted. In Duck, a completed turn is undone by returning the Duck first, then the chess piece.\n\nIf you undo a computer reply in Duck before lifting the Duck, first return the computer’s chess piece. Then follow the lights to return the Duck and your piece from the preceding turn.\n\nWhile Cancel Undo is available, select it to restore the forward move. If the Duck is in your hand, return it to its source before trying again. Finish all required returns before continuing play.",
  "@manualUndoBody": {
    "description": "Committed Duck Undo returns Duck then chess. An unfinished CPU reply before Duck pickup returns the CPU chess piece, then the previous human Duck and chess move. Cancel Undo is conditional; a held Duck must return to its source before retry."
  },
