  "boardLightsManualLink": "How Board lights and animation work",
  "manualLightsBody": "Open Connected at the top of the app to control brightness and Automatic brightness. In Setup, Board lights and animation controls the light-square LEDs and other lighting behavior. Automatic brightness is on by default. It blends the two light sensors to adjust the board to the room. Turn it off for a steady manual level; both sensors still take readings for diagnostics. Your choice is saved on the board.\n\nLevel 0 is near dark: essential cues stay dim and room light does not brighten them. Color detail is reduced and dim background squares may disappear at this level. With Automatic brightness off, level 8 requests the highest normal brightness. Power limits can reduce the actual output.\n\nWith Automatic brightness on, the slider sets the maximum; the lights dim below it in darker rooms. Turning Auto off uses the same saved level as steady manual brightness.",
